---
import:
  - undying-tide-base
  - undying-tide-presentation
  - undying-tide-creatures
requires:
  - regeneration
description: Jellyfish figure - the jellyfish bell pulses, its tentacles sway and stream, and its bell turns to its heading.
---

***implementation reqs***

- :Implementation: builds the :Jellyfish: figure in the Three.js scene as a full 3D `THREE.Group` with a translucent 3D dome mesh (`THREE.LatheGeometry` revolved 360° around the `y` axis with 3D depth across `z` equal to its width and 8 3D scallops around its lower rim) that pulses radially in all three axes (`bell.scale.set(pose.bellScale.x, pose.bellScale.y, pose.bellScale.x)` so `scale.z` pulses identically to `scale.x`) using a lit 3D material (`THREE.MeshPhysicalMaterial` or `THREE.MeshStandardMaterial`), a lit emissive 3D sphere mesh for the core and highlight, a `THREE.PointLight` in the palette's core colour, a horizontal 3D circular lower-rim ring (`THREE.TorusGeometry` or horizontal `THREE.TubeGeometry` around the circular rim in the `xz` plane at `y = -20`, never a flat 2D `z = 0` silhouette), 8 3D radial ribs (`THREE.TubeGeometry`) arching in 3D along meridians of the revolved dome surface (`x = r(y) cos(θ_i)`, `z = r(y) sin(θ_i)` at 8 evenly spaced azimuth angles `θ_i` around the `y` axis from 6 px below the top to the lower rim, never flat at `z = 0`), and 8 lit 3D tube meshes (`THREE.TubeGeometry` with `THREE.MeshStandardMaterial`) for the tentacles distributed in a 3D circle around the lower rim (`rimX = 15 cos(θ_i)`, `rimZ = 15 sin(θ_i)` at `θ_i = (i + 0.5) × π / 4`, with the 4 front tentacles at `z > 0` and the 4 back tentacles at `z < 0`, swaying and streaming in 3D `(x, y, z)`).
  - :UnitTests: of `src/game/render/jellyfish-figure.ts` assert the bell mesh uses `THREE.LatheGeometry` (with bounding-box depth across `z` of 40 px) and `THREE.MeshPhysicalMaterial` or `THREE.MeshStandardMaterial` (never `THREE.ShapeGeometry` or `THREE.MeshBasicMaterial`), that `applyJellyfishPose` scales the bell in 3D with `bell.scale.z === bell.scale.x`, that the rim and radial ribs span 3D depth across `z` (`boundingBox.max.z - boundingBox.min.z > 20`, never flat in the `xy` plane), that it includes a `THREE.PointLight` in the bell group, and that it places the 8 tentacles around the 3D circular rim with 4 having `z > 0` and 4 having `z < 0` using `THREE.MeshStandardMaterial`.

***functional specs***

# bell-pulse
The :Jellyfish: figure pulses: its bell narrows to 82% of its width and lengthens to 118% of its height, then relaxes out past its drawn size to 108% of its width and 94% of its height and settles back to its drawn size, once every 1.2 s, and once every 0.8 s while it swims or steers: while Space, Arrow Up, W, Arrow Down, S, Arrow Left, A, Arrow Right or D is held.
- Left and Right held together count as neither held, and Up and Down held together count as neither held.
- While it swims or turns, each contraction starts with a stroke of the :Jellyfish:, the gentle strokes of a turn included; a stroke that starts mid-pulse takes the bell into its contraction from where it stands, without a jump.
- The figure pulses about its centre; the :Jellyfish: circle stays radius 24.

# wavy-tentacles
The :Jellyfish: has 8 wavy tentacles in the palette's player tentacles colour, hanging from the lower rim of its bell, spread evenly along it, each moving on its own.
- From left to right they are 54, 60, 64, 68, 66, 62, 58 and 52 px long, sway once every 3.0, 3.6, 4.1, 3.3, 3.9, 4.4, 3.5 and 3.8 s, and start 0, 0.55, 0.3, 0.8, 0.15, 0.65, 0.4 and 0.9 of a cycle into their sway.
- Each sway is a wave running from the rim to the tip: 0 px across at the rim, growing to 28, 34, 26, 30, 36, 28, 34 and 30 px at the tip, the tip a whole cycle behind the rim, so each tentacle holds one full wave along its length.
- Each contraction of the bell's pulse draws every tip up to 12 px radially in towards the bell's vertical `y` axis, and they spread back as the bell relaxes; the bell's pulse scales `bell.scale.z` identically to `bell.scale.x` so the 3D dome contracts and expands symmetrically in 3D.
- A tentacle is a smooth 3D curve through at least 8 points in `(x, y, z)`, starting from its scallop's lowest point on the 3D circular lower rim (`rimX = 15 cos(θ_i)`, `rimZ = 15 sin(θ_i)` for `θ_i = (i + 0.5) × π / 4`) and tapering from 3 px wide at the rim to 1 px at the tip.
- Its bend follows a change of the :Jellyfish: velocity with a lag growing along it, reaching the tip 0.8 s after the rim, so the tips keep drifting the old way after it turns or stops.
- At rest they hang straight out of the lower rim, away from the bell's top; while it moves they bend from that line in 3D to stream out opposite its movement (towards the trailing camera when swimming forward), more the faster it moves, fully behind it at 240 px/s and above.
- When it stops, they swing back to hanging straight out of the lower rim over 1.5 s, easing out, never in one step.
- They are drawn beneath the bell around its 3D circular rim as lit `THREE.TubeGeometry` meshes (`THREE.MeshStandardMaterial`), with the 4 front tentacles at `z > 0` (`i = 0, 1, 2, 3`) and the 4 back tentacles at `z < 0` (`i = 4, 5, 6, 7`).

# bell-turns-to-heading
The :Jellyfish: bell is drawn turned to its :Heading: and tipped forward into its movement: while it swims it lies at `90`° to upright, its top pointing the way it swims along its :Heading: and `pitch` - level with Space alone, 45° down or up with Up or Down - and its lower rim and tentacles trailing straight back towards the camera; the tip grows with its speed (`forwardTiltDeg = 90 × min(1, hypot(vx, vy, vz) / 280)`, `jellyfish.rotation.x = ((pitch × min(1, hypot(vx, vy, vz) / 280) - forwardTiltDeg) × π) / 180`), upright at rest, and `jellyfish.rotation.z` banks with lateral velocity.
- The bell's 3D pulse, its core and every 3D mark drawn on it turn and tilt with it, and the 8 tentacles hang from its 3D circular lower rim as turned and tilted, keeping their sway, lag and 3D streaming opposite the velocity towards the camera.
- The line the tentacles hang along at rest, and bend from while it moves, turns and tilts with the bell: it runs out of the lower rim away from the bell's top as turned and tilted, never crossing through the bell.
- Once it has stopped, the forward tilt eases back to `0°` as the velocity slows to `0` and the tentacles swing back to hanging straight down when the bell is upright at rest.
- The bell is drawn at the :Heading: and 3D movement tilt alone: the :Jellyfish: collision circle stays radius 24.

# frilled-dome-bell
The :Jellyfish: bell is a 3D revolved frilled dome (`THREE.LatheGeometry` with `THREE.MeshPhysicalMaterial` or `THREE.MeshStandardMaterial`), 40 px wide across `x`, 40 px deep across `z`, and 46 px tall from its top to its lower rim, centred on the :Jellyfish: centre, as drawn before its pulse.
- The 3D dome is rounded at the top; its sides widen in 3D to their widest 8 px above the lower rim, then curve in to the circular lower rim, 34 px across in `x` and `z`.
- The lower rim is 8 equal 3D scallops around the circular rim, each curving 3 px down between its ends; the 8 tentacles hang one from the lowest point of each scallop around the 3D circle (`rimX = 15 cos(θ_i)`, `rimZ = 15 sin(θ_i)` at `y = -23`).
  - Each tentacle starts at its scallop's lowest point on the 3D circular rim, 23 px below the :Jellyfish: centre with the bell upright, and stays there as the bell pulses, turns and tilts; no tentacle starts inside the bell.
  - Every mark drawn along the bell's rim (the rim tube, Hard bell stroke and Quick regeneration shimmer) follows the 3D circular lower rim around the `y` axis in `(x, y, z)`, never a flat 2D `z = 0` silhouette loop.
- The rim of the bell is a 3D circular scalloped tube (`THREE.TubeGeometry` around the 3D lower rim in `(x, y, z)` with `boundingBox.max.z - boundingBox.min.z >= 30`), stroked 1.5 px in the palette's bell-rim colour; the 3D dome surface is shaded in the palette's bell colour at 30% opacity.
- 8 3D radial ribs (`THREE.TubeGeometry`) arch along 3D meridians of the revolved dome surface (`x = r(y) cos(θ_i)`, `z = r(y) sin(θ_i)` around the 3D dome) from 6 px below the top to the lower rim, 1 px wide in the bell-rim colour at 40% opacity.
- The core, a 3D lit sphere (`THREE.MeshStandardMaterial`) of radius 7 in the palette's core colour with its 3D core-highlight sphere and `THREE.PointLight` in the bell group, sits inside the dome on the bell's centre line 15 px below its top, visible through the translucent 3D bell.
- The :Jellyfish: circle stays radius 24.
